        "proteinName": "Neurogenic locus notch homolog protein 3",
        "mendelianRandomization": false,
        "omicsEvidence": [],
        "causalEvidenceSummary": "NOTCH3 is an established monogenic cause of cSVD (CADASIL), and this paper contributes NEW clinical variant-level data: two novel cases of heterozygous p.Arg1231Cys (EGFr domain 31, nominally low-risk) presenting with early-onset dementia, strokes, and extensive leukoencephalopathy. The authors argue these cases indicate higher-than-expected penetrance for this variant and call for functional evaluation, supporting a direct causal link between this NOTCH3 variant and hereditary small vessel disease rather than mere background citation.",
        "sourceQuote": "We report two cases of p.Arg1231Cys heterozygosity presenting with early-onset dementia, strokes, and extensive leukoencephalopathy."
      },
      {
        "symbol": "COL4A1",
        "pmid": "41001161",
        "confidence": 0.9,
        "gwasTraits": [
          "ICH-non-lobar",
          "cerebral-microbleeds",
          "lacunes"
        ],
        "proteinName": "Collagen type IV alpha-1 chain",
        "mendelianRandomization": false,
        "omicsEvidence": [],
        "causalEvidenceSummary": "New patient-level genetic data: two consanguineous Palestinian siblings with cSVD phenotypes (antenatal intracerebral/intraventricular hemorrhage, cerebral microhemorrhages, porencephalic cysts, and an incident lacunar infarct on follow-up MRI) were confirmed by genetic testing to carry the same COL4A1 variant (missense c.2707G>C, p.Gly903Arg), with segregation supported by an affected father with encephalomalacia. The paper adds mechanistic reasoning that glycine substitutions in the collagenous domain disrupt triple-helix formation, impairing basement membrane incorporation and producing fragility of small cerebral vessels, BBB leakage, and ER stress. Evidence is cSVD-specific (microbleeds, lacunar infarct, hemorrhage, leukoaraiosis), representing new monogenic variant evidence rather than a background citation.",
        "sourceQuote": "Genetic testing confirmed a COL4A1 missense mutation (c.2707G > C, p.Gly903Arg)."
      },
